{"step_index":103,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T18:08:35Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"@'\n# BhashaSetu AI (भाषासेतु AI)\n> **\"Every Child Learns Best in Their Mother Tongue\"**  \n> **Smart India Hackathon 2024 — Government of Jharkhand Track (Problem Statement #1628)**  \n> **Theme:** EdTech / Digital India / Inclusive Education\n\n---\n\n## 🌟 Executive Summary\n**BhashaSetu AI** is an AI-powered, offline-capable translation and vernacular pedagogy tool designed specifically for rural and tribal primary schools in Jharkhand. It bridges the critical language mismatch between state-appointed teachers (who speak Hindi/English) and primary school children (who speak indigenous tribal languages such as Santhali, Mundari, Ho, Kurukh, and Kharia).\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Key Features\n\n1. **Bilingual UI Switcher**: Complete site UI switches between **English** and **Hindi (हिन्दी)** instantaneously.\n2. **Offline-First Edge AI (0 kbps)**: Simulated 4-bit quantized IndicTrans2 and Whisper ASR edge models running locally on low-cost tablets with zero internet connectivity.\n3. **Interactive Working Translator**:\n   - Live bidirectional translation between Hindi, English, Bengali, Odia, Tamil, Telugu, and Jharkhand's tribal languages (**Santhali in Ol Chiki script**, **Mundari**, **Ho in Warang Chiti**, **Kurukh**, **Kharia**).\n   - One-click classroom scenario presets (Morning Greeting & Roll Call, Math Addition, Hygiene & Mid-Day Meal, Folk Tale Introduction, Science Observation).\n   - Microphone voice input simulation with animated soundwave visualizer.\n   - Realistic multi-stage pipeline loading animation (Acoustic tokenization -> Transformer alignment -> Native synthesis).\n   - Dual-script output: Native script (e.g. Ol Chiki glyphs) + Devanagari transliteration.\n   - Teacher's Romanized Phonetic pronunciation guide (empowering non-tribal teachers to speak the mother tongue directly).\n   - Multimodal contextual educational flashcard aid with relevant emoji pictograms.\n   - Synthetic speech audio playback and copy to clipboard.\n4. **How It Works & System Architecture**: 4-step classroom workflow and interactive 4-layer system architecture diagram.\n5. **National Sovereign Tech Stack**: Built around IndicTrans2, Whisper Indic, TensorFlow Lite, Bhashini NLTM API, and PWA offline storage.\n6. **Measurable Social Outcomes & Policy Alignment**: Real metrics mapped to **NEP 2020 §§4.11–4.13**, **UN SDG 4**, and **NIPUN Bharat**.\n7. **Pitch Video Showcase & 6-Member Team Grid**: Tailored for hackathon judging rounds.\n\n---\n\n## 💻 How to Run\n\nDouble-click `start.bat` or open `index.html` directly in any web browser (Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, Firefox, Brave, Safari).\nNo installation, no npm, and no external API keys are required.\n'@ | Out-File -FilePath \"README.md\" -Encoding utf8","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\bhashasetu-ai","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":3000,"toolAction":"Write README.md","toolSummary":"Create README.md documentation"}}]}
